   "id": "ai-spending-tech-selloff",
   "group": "United States",
   "headline": "Tech sell-off deepens on doubts that AI spending will pay off",
   "when": "Fri 30 Oct · US session",
   "what": "US stocks fell for a second day. The S&P 500 closed down 1.82% at 7,580.07 and the Nasdaq down 2.86%. Intel dropped about 29% at one point after warning it will burn cash this year. Nvidia fell around 4% and Coinbase 13% during the session. Alphabet had its worst day on record on Thursday. Separately, OpenAI is reported to have cut its funding target to up to $20 billion from $30 billion.",
   "why": "Your US exposure is mostly index funds and large tech, so they move with this theme. ES-US500RMF and K-USA-A(D) are priced at 28 Oct NAVs this morning. The S&P 500 is down about 2.1% since then, so that fall is not yet in your numbers. The dashboard refreshes again at 11:30.",
